INFO 8519 :: Page 41 :: 5 P. M. Louisville Ky. Jan. 14. 1865. Lvl. 14th 2 PM Hon. C. A. Dana, Wash. ---- arrived here last night nothing here from Thomas or Schofield . The telegh will not be open beyond Nashville till tomorrow . the necessary boats are ordered to rendezvous at Paducah . I go to Paducah tonight will be there tomorrow night & move up Tuesday unless counter orders come . it it decided about moving artillery ? the horses can be moved so far as the boats go without much difficulty Rivers all high & still rising slowly present prospects good telegraph can reach me at Paducah Signed Lewis B. Parsons Col. Chf of RRd Transptn dated 2 pm recd at 3 pm 9 P. M. City Pt. Jan 15. 1865 - 2 P. M. for the President U. S. . I send you by telegraph message from Jeff Davis & other despatches from Richmond Whig concerning the arrest of Ex Senator Foote . which is all the information I have on the subject any further information that I obtain will be sent you . What is likely to be done with him is difficult to conjecture . I suppose they will at farthest do nothing more than imprison him Signed US Grant Lt. Gen
