INFO 8521 :: Page 43 :: 410 PM Ft Monroe Va Jany 16th 1865 H'd Q'rs Army James 15th via Ft Monroe 16th for Gen Butler Washn . Genl I have the honor to forward you by telegraph the sounding at low tide on the centre line of the Dutch Gap canal all taken at 1 PM this day commencing at fifteen feet depth in the river at lower end of Canal & sounding at intervals of eighteen feet to fifteen feet depth of water in river at upper end of canal . I find , fifteen - twelve - eleven - thirteen - ten - ten and a half - nine and a half - nine - ten - nine & a half - nine - nine - nine & a quarter - nine - seven & a half - six - six - five - five - four - three & a half - three and a half - three & a half - three - three - two - two - two and a half - three - three & a half - four - four & a half - five - seven - ten - fifteen . Add three and a half feet to all these soundings for depth at daily high tide & eight feet for depth at highest water during recent freshet in James river . One hundred & fifty feet of the shallowest part is at low tide fifty three feet wide on surface of water in narrowest place . Very respect fully your obt servant &c . ---- L. L. Buckland Lieut Engr Ass't Eng'r
