INFO 7699 :: Page 41 :: 330 P. M. HdQrs A. P. Jan 15. 1865. 2 pm Capt G. K. Asst Adjt Genl ---- Can McGee find Chas Dillard a Scout formerly Employed in this Dept ---- If so have him found & sent to Col Sharp City Pt under guard on mail boat ---- can Mc - Gee recognize Charlotte Dillard Sister of above & when & where did he see her last ---- Jno. C. Babcock (3.40 P. M.) Hd. Qrs. A. of J. Jan 15. 1865. 230 P M. 15th for Secretary Navy ---- Blair accompanied by two commissioners from Alabama passed through here on their way to Washn. yesterday afternoon ---- Richmond papers of 14th state that our fleet had appeared off Wilmington & also state that it is rumored the bombardment had commenced Signed Arthur R Henry
